                <p><strong>Eligibility Criteria for scholarships that come under MP Scholarship:</strong></p>
                <h4><strong>1. Mukhyamantri Medhavi Vidyarthi Yojana, Madhya Pradesh</strong></h4>
                <p>This scholarship is for those students who have passed their&nbsp;<strong>12th with 75% or more&nbsp;</strong>from the state board and&nbsp;<strong>85% or more from CBSE/ICSE</strong>. The annual income should not exceed<strong>&nbsp;INR 6 Lakhs</strong>. If the candidate is an engineering student, then their&nbsp;<strong>JEE Mains Rank should be till 50,000 or less.&nbsp;</strong>Medical or dental students should have cleared their&nbsp;NEET<strong>&nbsp;exam.</strong>&nbsp;Law students should have cleared their&nbsp;<strong>CLAT exam and got into NLU.</strong></p>
                <h4><strong>2. Post Matric Scholarship Scheme for OBC Students, Madhya Pradesh</strong></h4>
                <p>The student should belong to the OBC Category, and family income should be<strong>&nbsp;less than 75,000/- for 100% scholarship&nbsp;</strong>and&nbsp;<strong>1,00,000 for 50% scholarship.</strong></p>
                <h4><strong>3. Mukhya Mantri Jan Kalyan Yojana (MMJKY), Madhya Pradesh</strong></h4>
                <p>If your parent is an unorganized workman under the&nbsp;<strong>department of Labour in Madhya Pradesh</strong>, then this scholarship is for you. This scholarship is for students getting into&nbsp;<strong>undergraduate, postgraduate, diploma, polytechnic, or any ITI stream</strong>.</p>
                <p>Students getting into engineering should have their<strong>&nbsp;JEE Mains ranks till 1,50,000 or below.&nbsp;</strong>Medical students should have qualified&nbsp;<strong>JIPMER&nbsp;</strong>or&nbsp;<strong>AIIMS&nbsp;</strong>examination for the&nbsp;<strong>BBS course</strong>. Law students have to qualify for the CLAT exam and got into one of the NLUs.</p>
                <h4><strong>4. Post Matric Scholarship Scheme for the SC Students, Madhya Pradesh</strong></h4>
                <p>After the secondary level, students belonging to the Scheduled Caste category can apply for this scholarship.</p>
                <h4><strong>5. Post Matric Scholarship Scheme for the ST Students, Madhya Pradesh</strong></h4>
                <p>This scholarship is for the students belonging to the Scheduled Tribe category. If the annual family income from all the sources is&nbsp;<strong>less than INR 2,50, 000</strong>&nbsp;then you are eligible for&nbsp;<strong>100% scholarship</strong>, and if it&rsquo;s between&nbsp;<strong>INR 2,50,000 to 6,00,000,&nbsp;</strong>then you are eligible for&nbsp;<strong>50% scholarship.</strong></p>
